# =============================================================
#  REDIRECTS  (Netlify reads this file automatically)
#  -------------------------------------------------------------
#  The old website was built as separate .aspx pages. The new one
#  is a single page with sections, so every old address is pointed
#  at the matching section here.
#
#  WHY THIS MATTERS: those old addresses are the ones Google has
#  indexed and that people have bookmarked. Without these lines
#  they would show "page not found" after the switchover and we
#  would lose our search ranking. With them, visitors and Google
#  are passed straight to the right place.
#
#  The "301" means "moved permanently", which is what tells Google
#  to transfer the old page's ranking to the new one.
# =============================================================

# ── Old .aspx pages → matching section of the new single page ──
/Default.aspx              /               301
/default.aspx              /               301
/about.aspx                /#about         301
/About.aspx                /#about         301
/venue.aspx                /#meetings      301
/a-typical-meeting.aspx    /#meetings      301
/calendar.aspx             /#meetings      301
/faqs.aspx                 /#faq           301
/FAQs.aspx                 /#faq           301
/contact-us.aspx           /#contact       301
/how-do-i-join.aspx        /#join          301
/links.aspx                /#contact       301

# Toastmaster Tips has no equivalent on the new site yet. Sending it
# to the meetings section for now; if that content gets recreated,
# point this line at its new home instead.
/toastmaster-tips.aspx     /#meetings      301

# Note: every page that existed on the old site is listed above. If any
# other old address turns up later, add a line for it here in the same
# format. Anything unlisted shows the friendly 404 page, which links home.
